{t:Back in Black}
{artist: AC/DC}
{key: D}
Based on <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s5usS-vh3Zg" target="_blank">Jb Lessons</a> and <a href="https://youtu.be/cpn8g-DV-rM">Ukulele Cheats</a>
{st: Written by Angus Young, Malcolm Young, and Brian Johnson.}

Notes:
p=Pull Off
b=Bend 1/2 step

{c: "pull off riff"}
{sot}
-3-p0-------------
------3-p0--------
------------2b-p0-
------------------
{eot}

{c: "slide riff"}
{sot}
------------------------
-0---0---0---0----------
---1---2---3---4-slide-- (use fist finger on all)
------------------------
{eot}
{c: "chorus note"}
In the chorus only play the root of the chord for [C]*

{c: Verse}
         
[A] Back in black, 
[G][G][G] I hit the sack
[D][D][D] I've been too long, 
I'm glad to be back
{pull off riff}

Yes, I'm [A] let loose
[G][G][G] From the noose
[D][D][D] That's kept me hanging about
{slide riff}

I've been [A] looking at the sky
[G][G][G] 'Cause it's gettin' me high
[D][D][D] Forget the hearse 'cause I never die
{pull off riff}

I got [A] nine lives
[G][G][G] Cat's eyes
[D][D][D] Abusin' every one of them and running wild
{slide riff}

